session:pr138Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Adds NetworkPolicy::AllowList(Vec<String>) variant to ingress::NetworkPolicy that permits SPARQL LOAD only when the URL string starts with one of the configured prefixes SSRF hardening from #135 (IP blocking, cross-host redirect policy, 64 MiB cap) still applies on top of the prefix check Removes Copy from NetworkPolicy (required by Vec<String>); all implicit copy sites updated to .clone() Extends parse_network_policy in src/main.rs to accept allow:<prefix1>[,<prefix2>…] syntax All existing match arms on NetworkPolicy updated to handle the new variant Changed files | File | Change | |---|---| | ingress/src/network_policy.rs | Add AllowList variant; remove Copy | | sparql_endpoint/src/sparql_update.rs | fetch_rdf(url, policy) signature; prefix check; merge Allow\\|AllowList arm | | sparql_parser/src/execute.rs | Add AllowList arm for SERVICE handling | | jsonld_parser/src/lib.rs | Add AllowList arm for @context URL handling | | src/main.rs | parse_network_policy supports allow:<prefixes>; updated doc-comment | | sparql_endpoint/src/query.rs, dataset_routes.rs, graph_store.rs, lib.rs | Add .clone() at all network_policy usage sites | | sparql_endpoint/tests/allowlist.rs | New integration test file (6 tests) | | sparql_endpoint/src/sparql_update.rs (tests) | 3 new unit tests for fetch_rdf prefix logic |" ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:138 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr138 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
